SUMMARY:“Is AA Still Self-Supporting?” Virtual Panel Discussion
DESCRIPTION:“Is AA Still Self-Supporting?” Virtual Panel Discussion\n\nThe California Northern Coastal Area (CNCA 06) of Alcoholics Anonymous is hosting a virtual panel discussion exploring the topic of self-support within AA\, addressing declining contributions and rising expenses.\n \n\nThe event will take place online on Thursday\, June 11\, 2026\, from 6:00–7:30 p.m. Pacific Time. Following the panel presentations\, attendees are invited to participate in an area sharing session.\n \nFeatured Speakers\n\nJohn W. — Treasurer\, General Service Board\nJoe N. — Chair\, NorCal Hospitals & Institutions Committee\nNikki T. — Past Board Member\, SF & Marin Intergroup\n\nMeeting Information\n\nMeeting ID: 817-7862-8065\nPasscode: 1935\n\n\nThe event is free and open to all. Attendees may also join using the QR code provided on the flyer.
URL:https://sonomacountyaa.org/event/is-aa-still-self-supporting-virtual-panel-discussion/
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://sonomacountyaa.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/CNCA-Self-Support-Flyer-EN-V2.png
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR